            <fr:title text="Displayed Category">Displayed Category</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>A <html:em>displayed category</html:em> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {\mathcal {D}}]]></fr:tex> over a <fr:link href="/sss-00EC/" title="Category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00EC/" display-uri="sss-00EC" type="local">base category</fr:link>
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> packages the data of a category that "lies over" <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex>: each object
and each morphism of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> is equipped with a fiber of objects and morphisms
displayed atop it. It consists of
<html:ol><html:li>For each object <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x : \mathcal {c}_{0}]]></fr:tex>, a <html:em>type</html:em> of displayed objects
  <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {\mathcal {D}}_{x}]]></fr:tex> lying over <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x]]></fr:tex>. We write <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {x} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{x}]]></fr:tex>
  for a displayed object over <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
  <html:li>For each morphism <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f : \mathcal {C} {\mathopen {}\left (x , y\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> and displayed objects
  <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {x} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{x}]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {y} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{y}]]></fr:tex>, a <html:em>set</html:em>
  of displayed morphisms <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {y}\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> lying over <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex>. We write such
  a displayed morphism <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {g} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {y}\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> as
  <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {g} : \overline {x} \to _{f} \overline {y}]]></fr:tex> or
  <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {x} \overset {\overline {g}}{\to _{f}} \overline {y}]]></fr:tex>, subscripting the
  arrow with the base morphism <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex> it lies over.</html:li>
  <html:li>A displayed composition operation. For <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f : x \to  y]]></fr:tex> and
  <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[g : y \to  z]]></fr:tex> with displayed morphisms
  <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {f} : \overline {x} \to _{f} \overline {y}]]></fr:tex> and
  <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {g} : \overline {y} \to _{g} \overline {z}]]></fr:tex>, there is a displayed
  morphism <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {f} \star  \overline {g} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f \star  g}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {z}\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> lying
  over the composite <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f \star  g]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
  <html:li>For each <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {x} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{x}]]></fr:tex>, a displayed identity
  <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathsf {id}_{\overline {x}} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{\mathsf {id}_{x}}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {x}\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> lying over <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathsf {id}_{x}]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
  <html:li>Left-unitality, displayed: for all <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {f} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {y}\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>,
  a heterogeneous equality
  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\overline {\mathsf {idL}_{f}} : \mathsf {id}_{\overline {x}} \star  \overline {f} =_{\mathsf {idL}_{f}} \overline {f}]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li>Right-unitality, displayed: for all <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {f} : \overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {y}\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>,
  a heterogeneous equality
  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\overline {\mathsf {idR}_{f}} : \overline {f} \star  \mathsf {id}_{\overline {y}} =_{\mathsf {idR}_{f}} \overline {f}]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li>Associativity, displayed: for all <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {f}]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {g}]]></fr:tex>,
  <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {h}]]></fr:tex> over <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f : x \to  y]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[g : y \to  z]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[h : z \to  w]]></fr:tex>,
  a heterogeneous equality
  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\overline {\mathsf {assoc}_{f , g , h}} : {\mathopen {}\left (\overline {f} \star  {\mathopen {}\left (\overline {g} \star  \overline {h}\right )\mathclose {}}\right )\mathclose {}} =_{\mathsf {assoc}_{f , g , h}} {\mathopen {}\left ({\mathopen {}\left (\overline {f} \star  \overline {g}\right )\mathclose {}} \star  \overline {h}\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex></html:li></html:ol></html:p>
            <html:p>Because the type <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {\mathcal {D}}_{f}{\mathopen {}\left (\overline {x} , \overline {y}\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> of displayed morphisms depends on
the base morphism <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex>, the two sides of each displayed law inhabit
<html:em>different</html:em> displayed hom-sets — those indexed by the two sides of the
corresponding base-category equation. Each displayed law is therefore a
<html:em>heterogeneous equality</html:em> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[a =_{p} b]]></fr:tex>: a path from <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[a]]></fr:tex> to <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[b]]></fr:tex> lying
over the base path <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[p]]></fr:tex>, rather than an equation within a single fixed set.</html:p>
            <html:p>Concretely, this definition models <fr:link href="https://github.com/agda/cubical/blob/master/Cubical/Categories/Displayed/Base.agda" type="external">the one used in the Cubical standard
library</fr:link>
<fr:link href="/cubicalagdalib/" title="The Cubical Agda Library" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/cubicalagdalib/" display-uri="cubicalagdalib" type="local">[cubicalagdalib]</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p>
A displayed category is to a category as a dependent type is to a
context. In this way,
displayed categories are effectively <html:em>dependent categories</html:em>, as
we present the structure of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {\mathcal {D}}]]></fr:tex> as a category parametrized
by the structure of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
            <html:p>Displayed categories were introduced by Ahrens and Lumsdaine
<fr:link href="/ahrens-lumsdaine-2019/" title="Displayed Categories" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/ahrens-lumsdaine-2019/" display-uri="ahrens-lumsdaine-2019" type="local">[ahrens-lumsdaine-2019]</fr:link>. The point is that a displayed category over
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> is equivalent to the data of a category <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {D}]]></fr:tex> together with a
functor <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F : \mathcal {D} \to  \mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex>, but presented as families indexed by the
objects and morphisms of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> — so that constructions like Grothendieck
fibrations can be defined without ever invoking equality of objects.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
